{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/13389-slices-of-mundanity-jimb-s-essay-journal","id":13389,"title":"Slices of Mundanity: JimB's Essay Journal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T07:37:54-08:00","id":13389,"title":"Slices of Mundanity: JimB's Essay Journal","content":"Because why not, that's why.<br /> <br /> At work this morning, we had a long-delayed ethics meeting. Five out of the fifty or so of us get together to discuss ethical issues our company may have faced in the last month. No one could think of anything, so I asked if a patient of ours, a manipulative man who had been trying to score drugs off us and quit our care two weeks after signing on because we wouldn't give them to him, had constituted an ethical issue for us. There was a bit of desultory conversation on the topic, and it was decided that no, we did everything we could, and even if there had been an ethical issue, he was no longer on our service and there was no way to follow up on any hypothetical issue, so there was no reason filling out any paperwork over it.<br /> <br /> I feel like there are a lot of tacit admissions in that &quot;even if&quot; and &quot;no reason&quot; bit, but the issue was closed, so I mentally shrugged and verbally wisecracked, &quot;As the Buddha said while sitting beneath the tree, it ain't our fucking problem any more, right?&quot; I wasn't actually making a point or anything; I just thought (and think) it's a funny line, so I put it out there and waited for the applause.<br /> <br /> It didn't come. My boss and her boss were silent, the chaplain tried running with it (&quot;Were his legs crossed when he said it?&quot;), and the social worker burst into peals of laughter she had to smother behind her hand. I was a little annoyed, but then, I should have known it would be like that, so I mentally shrugged again and chalked it up as a reminder that whenever I think a joke I've written is hilarious, it's an invariable rule of life that other people will only think it's okay. Oh well.<br /> <br /> My boss and her boss continued messing around with something, I think a patient referral or something, and I went into the supply room to dick around because there was no reason for me to leave the office for another forty-five minutes at that time (fifteen now). As I was coming out, my boss's boss pulled me aside and murmured in my ear, &quot;Refrain from using <i>that word</i>. It's inappropriate.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was a very near thing. I almost said it. It was right on my tongue before my self-interest, which had apparently been napping on the job, started awake, flung itself in a panicked leap from its chair, and grabbed the words right on the tip of my tongue so I could acquiesce, &quot;As you say,&quot; instead of giving him the annoyed, dismissive response that was my instinct. I did <i>not</i> tell him, &quot;Oh, fuck off.&quot;<br /> <br /> That was probably for the best, heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:21:14-08:00","id":13607,"title":"","content":"I keep wanting to start something like one of these but I highly doubt I'm interesting enough or write well enough to have a thread dedicated to myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:24:58-08:00","id":13615,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about being interesting. There was once an eight-month lull in the previous iteration of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:28:52-08:00","id":13618,"title":"","content":"yeah but mine will just sound like whining. woe as me shit. That's what for the journal is for huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:58:36-08:00","id":13633,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, yes. Why not? Venting usually feels liberating and other people dealing with similar issues could read it and relate and feel they are not alone in those feelings. Everybody wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:02:17-08:00","id":13750,"title":"","content":"One of my first patients upon coming to work for hospice was vaguely, sorta-but-not-really related to me. My mom's brother's ex-wife's aunt, I think. Doesn't matter. The story isn't about her relation to me. I never knew her, and she never knew me. By the time I'd met her, she'd already been consumed by some sort of undifferentiated (if only to us in hospice; back then, the qualifications for hospice care were much more lax) dementia, and a year of me visiting her wasn't enough for her to ever recognize me. Every time I went to her room to visit her, she'd stare up at me from her bed with an expression of fear that would have crossed into panic if not for the confusion marring her every thought; she was too far away from understanding what fear was to be able to build up a panic.<br /> <br /> She was tiny, and skeletal. Each limb was eternally wrapped first in a layer of gauze, then in Ace bandages, from trunk to tip because her muscles and fatty tissue had wasted away to the points that she was basically nothing but skin over bones, and her skin would tear just from rubbing the knobby protrusions of the very joints under her flesh. I eventually got to a point where I was skilled enough to bathe her without her bleeding, though, and I suppose I should be proud of that, though I'd forgotten the fact of her physical condition until just now as I wrote this. It's her mental state that I remember, her inability to process any kind of input or even her own feelings because the connections were down inside her brain. Messages were not going where they needed to go.<br /> <br /> Naturally, this meant she couldn't speak. In fact, there was only one sound she could vocalize. She never made any different noise that I can recall hearing. The only thing she was capable of issuing from her mouth...I'd spell it &quot;mairm,&quot; I suppose. High pitched, a little gravelly from her smoking years, and turned up at the end like it was a question or a plea, like she was saying, &quot;Will you please help me?&quot; What help she wanted, I can only guess. Probably to not be hurt.<br /> <br /> That was four or five years ago. Time rolls on, and you--or at least, I--forget things I don't need to remember any more. Disused, they drop silently into the dark waters at the bottom of the well of my memory, but sometimes, things float unbidden back up to the top. I remember things I don't really need any more, and once they come up, they float insistently at the top of my mind; I can force them under the water, but their buoyancy keeps them rising, so all day, I have been hearing an old woman begging me in my head:<br /> <br /> <i>Mairm?<br /> <br /> Mairm?<br /> <br /> Mairm?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:58:50-08:00","id":13999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/13389-slices-of-mundanity-jimb-s-essay-journal?p=13618#post13618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah but mine will just sound like whining. woe as me shit. That's what for the journal is for huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never underestimate the psychological value of getting shit off your chest, even if it's just to a piece of paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}